{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "fc", "rep": 209, "hyps": [{"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "At very small learning rates Adam underfits within 243 epochs, so increasing the rate helps far more than elsewhere (e.g. probes 32, 64, 65)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "At already-large learning rates a further increase causes divergence and large accuracy drops (probes 33, 67, 98)."}, {"edit_param": "alpha", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "alpha", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "When L2 is already strong, raising it further over-regularizes and sharply reduces accuracy (probe 11), whereas at small alpha the edit is near-neutral."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Larger batches reduce gradient noise and stabilize training at unstable high learning rates (probes 18, 63, 97)."}, {"edit_param": "batch_size", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "lower", "why": "With a tiny learning rate, fewer updates per epoch from larger batches worsens underfitting (probes 60, 61)."}, {"edit_param": "width", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "Wider networks fit faster and compensate for slow optimization at low learning rates (probes 41, 68, 69)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deeper networks are more prone to instability and divergence under high learning rates (probes 51, 75, 100)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "batch_size", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "higher", "why": "Large batches give fewer optimizer steps, so a higher learning rate is more beneficial (probes 27, 65)."}, {"edit_param": "depth", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "learning_rate_init", "cond_band": "low", "direction": "higher", "why": "Extra depth adds capacity and effective step size that helps underfit, slowly-trained models (probes 72, 73)."}, {"edit_param": "learning_rate_init", "edit_dir": "up", "cond_param": "depth", "cond_band": "high", "direction": "lower", "why": "Three-layer networks are less tolerant of larger learning rates than shallow ones, so raising the rate hurts more (probes 29, 87)."}], "tok": 27088, "bad": 0, "probes": [[[4, 4, 1, 4, 4], 0, "up"], [[4, 1, 1, 4, 4], 0, "up"], [[4, 8, 1, 4, 4], 0, "up"], [[4, 4, 0, 4, 4], 0, "up"], [[4, 4, 2, 4, 4], 0, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 1, 4], 0, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 8, 4], 0, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 1], 0, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 8], 0, "up"], [[1, 4, 1, 4, 4], 0, "up"], [[8, 4, 1, 4, 4], 0, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 4], 1, "up"], [[1, 4, 1, 4, 4], 1, "up"], [[8, 4, 1, 4, 4], 1, "up"], [[4, 4, 0, 4, 4], 1, "up"], [[4, 4, 2, 4, 4], 1, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 1, 4], 1, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 8, 4], 1, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 1], 1, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 8], 1, "up"], [[4, 1, 1, 4, 4], 1, "up"], [[4, 8, 1, 4, 4], 1, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 4], 3, "up"], [[1, 4, 1, 4, 4], 3, "up"], [[8, 4, 1, 4, 4], 3, "up"], [[4, 1, 1, 4, 4], 3, "up"], [[4, 8, 1, 4, 4], 3, "up"], [[4, 4, 0, 4, 4], 3, "up"], [[4, 4, 2, 4, 4], 3, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 1], 3, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 8], 3, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 1, 4], 3, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 8, 4], 3, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[1, 4, 1, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[8, 4, 1, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[4, 1, 1, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[4, 8, 1, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[4, 4, 0, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[4, 4, 2, 4, 4], 4, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 1, 4], 4, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 8, 4], 4, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 1], 4, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 8], 4, "up"], [[4, 4, 1, 4, 4], 2, "up"], [[1, 4, 1, 4, 4], 2, "up"], [[8, 4, 1, 4, 4], 2, "up"], [[4, 1, 1, 4, 4], 2, "up"], [[4, 8, 1, 4